  "selection_rationale": "Bernoulli NB is deployed. It also has the best macro F1. Three reasons for the choice: (1) its decision decomposes exactly into per-symptom log-odds, which is what makes the explanation panel a true attribution rather than a LIME/SHAP-style approximation; (2) unlike Multinomial NB it scores symptom *absence*, so the output of the NegEx/ConText layer -- symptoms the user explicitly denied -- is usable evidence rather than merely omitted; (3) it fits in milliseconds, keeping the whole pipeline reproducible on a laptop. Both Naive Bayes variants are saved, and AROGYA_MODEL switches between them.",
